    "turn_text": "But we've seen everything from the Safe Banking Act to multi tens of billions of dollars of bills being spent. through suspension. On the suspension calendar. And you have to get, this is one of my problems with Kevin, is you have to get the minority leader and the majority leader have to agree what goes on the suspension calendar. Exactly. So we change that. So those things are good. Then we move into the other thing. And this is really critical because we're kind of there now. And that is the budget process to try to get it to a more normalized budget process. So for instance, on debt ceiling, This is not in the rules packages, but this is one of the agreements is that we have to get some kind of assurance that you're going to actually reduce spending, federal spending, before you can vote for a debt ceiling increase. And the reason for that is because we got 31 trillion, in the last 12 years we've gone from 11 trillion to 30, almost 32 trillion dollars in debt. And we just keep raising the debt ceiling. Why? Because it's easier to do that than to balance a budget. It's easier",
